the the purpose for this specific location for us is that we have excess demand at our existing facility with no more space for machines um if any of you've gone by that facility on a Monday uh which is our fabulous 50s and upday um limited parkings available we know when we add the bowling alley which is uh going to be complete November one is our Target date to be open uh you're going to have a very very busy facility and there may be a lot of our customers that would prefer to go somewhere where it's easier to walk in than park at the back of the parking lot and compete with Bowlers and people that want to go to the arcade Etc so

um we do work with industry experts we have a third-party consulting firm called racing Resource Inc who has a good feel for the national pulse of historic horse racing and What markets can support um The Entity that ultimately supervises saturation which is what you're talking about is the Wildman Gaming Commission by Statute for us to receive a permit they have to determine that the market is not saturated um they did make that determination in this specific for this specific location I believe mostly based on uh the study that we submitted from racing Resource Group um and part of the study from racing Resource Group was based on basically our own customer player data and the projections of the use for the facility uh

the we we probably easily could have permitted that facility for it's currently permitted for 200 machines persing itself we could have gone for 300 or 325 and it probably would have supported that what that would have required us to do is eliminate some of the other entertainment options that we wanted as part of the construction project so instead of doing that and adding more gaming to that we looked for a geographically close location but also far enough away and easier Ingress and egress for people that would prefer the pure uh historic horse racing experience as opposed to the mixed entertainment facility that we're going to have at persing so it's two different product offerings um

I did explain on Monday and for your constituents uh it's probably important for them to know that the uh state of Wyoming through the gaming commission is currently performing a Statewide saturation study with consultants and pending the result of that study which is supposed to come out this fall I am sure that the gaming commission will be looking at uh different ways and have different data points for what they permit in the future so I don't have a a crystal ball for how that study going to shake out I've read other studies that other states have done um I would acknowledge that uh you know this community much like Casper is probably close to that point um

but at the same time I I believe we got permitted by the county and the gaming commission on the idea that this is to serve our existing customer base who prefers our product rather than um the idea that we're going to bring new people to the market it's just simply we have uh excess demand in our existing facility that we can't support in the square footage we have thanks for that explanation much appreciated follow question for Mr Ridgeway um I wasn't at that meeting on Monday but I have um been been privy to the information um Mr Ridgeway my question is and I don't certainly don't want to put you on the spot and um

